; --- 37E: the way to the Ashfall Homestead --------------------------------------
; The cottage that stood here until 37E was `bld_cottage.glb` -- a sealed 4.8 m mesh you could not
; enter -- beside a ROOFLESS pen of grey BoxMesh walls holding the stash and two greybox pillars.
; The whole holding moved to its own cell east of the Embermarket, where it is a house you walk into.
;
; ⚠️ WHAT STAYS BEHIND IS A SIGNPOST, AND IT IS NOT DECORATION. The deed post moved with the house,
; so nothing in the square would otherwise tell a player a house exists at all -- and a sink nobody
; can find is a sink nobody spends into. This is 37D's own lesson (it moved the deed OUT of the
; middle of the square and had to leave the player a reason to walk to it) applied one cell further.
;
; BuildingSW keeps bld_cottage_modular: it is a generic town house and always was.

[node name="HomesteadSign" type="Node3D" parent="Nav"]
transform = Transform3D(-0.1881, 0, -0.5168, 0, 0.55, 0, 0.5168, 0, -0.1881, 51, 0, 27.5)

[node name="Model" parent="Nav/HomesteadSign" instance=ExtResource("rp_lm_waystone")]


; Hesk the Wayfarer (Phase 38J) — the town's first VendorComponent, and the first merchant who is not
; always here. He is in the square one day in four and trades 09:00-17:00 on the day he is; both live on
; shop.ember_crown.traveller, where --validate can read them.
;
; The VendorComponent route rather than 38E's dialogue effect, and deliberately: an entity gets ONE
; interactable, so the three resident merchants had to hang trade off a dialogue choice to keep their
; quest conversations. Hesk has no conversation to protect, so the component is simply the right shape —
; this is the placement CLAUDE.md has been promising it since 38A.
;
; No ScheduleComponent. He does not walk a routine; he is either in town or he is not, and that is a pure
; function of WorldClock.Day rather than a destination to walk to.
;
; ⚠️ His ShopId lives in this .tscn and is therefore UNVALIDATED — a typo gives no prompt at all rather
; than an error, the same trap PropertyStorageComponent.PropertyId carries. If he is ever silently
; unusable in game, check that field before anything else.

